# Visitor city

The catalog suggests a Belarus city from the visitor IP. The lookup stays on our server.

## Library

Use `ip-location-api` with the free GeoLite2 City database (`language: ru`, `smallMemory: true`, `licenseKey: redist`). Database files live in `data/geoip/` and are not committed. Refresh them with `npm run geoip:update`.

Do not call ip-api, ipinfo, ipstack, or any other hosted geolocation API to resolve a city. A public IP echo (such as ipify) is allowed only when the request itself has no public address, so the server can look that IP up locally.

## What to store

Match the GeoLite2 city to `BELARUS_CITIES` in `src/lib/catalog/city-taxonomy.ts`. If the IP is not in Belarus, or the place is not in that list, leave the city empty.

Persist the chosen or detected place in the `trenio_place` cookie. The cookie stores the settlement name, not the IP.

## Search form

The homepage hero, the header, 403, 404, and an empty search result use one form: `CatalogSearchForm`.

Sport suggestions come from `src/lib/catalog/sport-taxonomy.ts` (category labels, sport labels, and aliases). Do not keep a second sport list for that field.

The city field shows the detected or saved settlement. When none is known, it shows `Минск`. Do not pick another fallback city. Sport category filters use that same city.

```ts
// wrong: ask a third party for the city
const city = await fetch(`https://ipapi.co/${ip}/city`);

// right: local database, then the taxonomy
const hit = await lookup(ip);
const city = hit?.country === "BY" ? canonicalCity(hit.city) : null;
```
